en Its Graph" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096708 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186096506 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096708 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "5e182f71-db24-5c29-9c8b-2fc4b5ab5dd8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096904 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096904 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096904 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096904 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096904 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096904 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096904 #edb/ref 1045 "Calculating Intercepts of Parabolas" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096904 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186097633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096904 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096904 #edb/ref 1050 720.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186096904 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "f97acdea-187e-5327-a13f-1e14931b5e5f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097117 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186094675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097117 #edb/ref 1069 "q-14242" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097117 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/d4/d457bfe2ac8b0a86da15e2c34704ae5011a58ad8c148905aa1df12a674544f6c.png)\n\nWhat are the $y$-intercepts of the parabola shown above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097117 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d128bb5c-b2a0-55d9-a9bb-7094e5734308" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097571 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097572 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097571 #edb/ref 1061 19720 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097571 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "47e80884-1762-5551-9161-e2231dbed002" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097571 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097855 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097572 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097572 #edb/ref 1061 19721 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097572 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "fd6bd854-7c41-5db8-95d8-5be58a99e006" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097572 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096706 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097573 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097571 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097573 #edb/ref 1061 19724 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097573 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "003b2c9e-f558-5f16-ae29-70cb592bdea5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097573 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096707 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097574 #edb/ref 1061 19725 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097574 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "82273a54-9ebb-549c-bc34-a98726936b3c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097574 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096708 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097633 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097573 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097633 #edb/ref 1061 23091 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097633 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3eccc6e2-615b-5126-b1a2-9f9bb514c40d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097633 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097868 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097855 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we want to know what are the $x$-intercepts of the parabola below.\n\n![](images/5d/5d3493115eb11315849d3d7c247b9f63a399c6ab7ba2c226b0b84958a47d3a21.png)\n\nThen, we proceed as follows: \n\nFirst, we find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has its vertex at $\\displaystyle\\left(\\frac 32, -1\\right)$ and passes through the point $\\displaystyle\\left(1,-\\frac 34\\right).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^2 = 4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k) = \\left(\\dfrac 32, -1\\right)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =4p(y+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $\\displaystyle\\left(1,-\\frac 34\\right),$ we substitute $x= 1$ and $y=-\\dfrac34$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =4p(-\\frac{3}{4}+1) \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & =4p(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =(y+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y= 0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =(0+1) \\\\ {(x-\\frac{3}{2})}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x-\\frac{3}{2} & =\\pm 1 \\\\ x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\pm 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are $\\dfrac12$ and $\\dfrac52.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097855 #edb/ref 1065 3484 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097855 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "04c720cc-0a5d-5a6c-acf5-65c378ef274b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097855 #edb/ref 1067 "Calculating the Intercepts of a Parabola Given a Graph of the Parabola" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097868 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's consider the parabola $(x-1)^2 = \\dfrac 1 2 (y+3) ,$ shown below.\n\n![](images/bb/bbe360c9580cab435e5b737c80c5381f039d1871250cdae3c16bc686e3d0a53d.png)\n\nTo calculate the $y$-intercept of the parabola (shown as the point $A$ in the diagram), we set $x=0$ and solve for $y.$ In our case, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(y+3) \\\\ (0-1)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(y+3) \\\\ (-1)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(y+3) \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{1}{2}(y+3) \\\\ 2 & =y+3 \\\\ y & =2-3 \\\\ y & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the coordinates of the $y$-intercept are $(0,-1).$\n\nOn the other hand, to find the $x$-intercepts (shown as the points $B$ and $C$ in the diagram), we set $y=0$ and solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(y+3) \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}(0+3) \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}} \\\\ x & =1\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the coordinates of $B$ are $\\left(1-\\sqrt{\\dfrac{3}{2}},0\\right)$ and the coordinates of $C$ are $\\left(1+\\sqrt{\\dfrac{3}{2}},0\\right).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097868 #edb/ref 1065 3905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097868 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "f9511803-ede3-5b03-b34f-87d1bb050901" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097868 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291324 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291324 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291324 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9f83b49c-5263-5a91-8e87-dd8dccdaf781" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291377 #edb/ref 1080 "-5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291377 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291377 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ab9359e1-2230-572b-b145-165bd7eeb22a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291453 #edb/ref 1080 "-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291453 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186291453 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "bf229ea4-be5b-5001-9fc2-49258187ce94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292378 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292378 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292378 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292378 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186291377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292378 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d38bb03c-5f69-54cf-9a38-955ba1cb544f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292453 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291324 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292453 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292453 #edb/ref 1077 "field-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292453 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186291324 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292453 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e5adab7c-e4c7-5d86-8e1b-e14e115b5f92" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292510 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186291453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292510 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292510 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292510 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186291453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292510 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f7860a9b-7728-5971-a35a-bae3745118ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292533 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186292378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292533 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186292453 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292533 #edb/ref 1069 "q-251784" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292533 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292533 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/af/afb7abacdffafd634165fd1f35868878b2bc420df6a173b48f6a17c7638f7dec.png)\n\n**From left to right**, the **exact values** of the $x$-intercepts of the parabola shown above are{{field-1}}\nand \n{{field-2}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292533 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3651a6f9-db8c-55ba-9b38-b5a076f97109" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292533 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-3,4)$ and passes through the point $(0,-5).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(-3,4)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2} & =4p(y-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(0,-5),$ we substitute $x=0$ and $y=-5$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0+3)^{2} & =4p(-5-4) \\\\ 9 & =4p(-9) \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2} & =-(y-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2} & =-(0-4) \\\\ (x+3)^{2} & =4 \\\\ x+3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{4} \\\\ x & =\\pm 2-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, from left to right, the $x$-intercepts are $-5$  and $-1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292534 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186292510 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292534 #edb/ref 1069 "q-251796" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292534 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292534 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/ce/cec5eacc688d3c3a619aeb6ede2b1c9f9290b8045699259d4c1d933ecefd1835.png)\n\nThe value of the $y$-intercept of the parabola shown above  is{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292534 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c0acb67a-a7e6-5061-89d3-c3088fc5fb2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186292534 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(4,-6)$ and passes through the point $(-2,3).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k),\n$$\n\nand substituting $(h,k)=(4,-6)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(x-4)^{2}=4p(y+6).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-2,3),$ we substitute $x=-2$ and $y=3$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2-4)^{2} & =4p(3+6) \\\\ 36 & =4p(9) \\\\ p & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-4)^{2} & =4(y+6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we substitute $x=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-4)^{2} & =4(y+6) \\\\ 16 & =4(y+6) \\\\ 4 & =y+6 \\\\ y & =4-6 \\\\ y & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $y$-intercept is $-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339346 #edb/ref 1080 "$(0,\\sqrt{3})$ and $(0,-\\sqrt{3})$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339346 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339346 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "18731f91-5a2b-5b17-a387-eb4cc9a4d188" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339410 #edb/ref 1080 "There are no intersection points" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339410 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339410 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "20d59ae8-b207-56f8-a181-059ef32b89f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339439 #edb/ref 1080 "$-\\sqrt{6}-1$ and $-\\sqrt{6}+1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339439 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339439 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "23d76beb-d71a-5dfa-94a8-e101972d6f15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339524 #edb/ref 1080 "$-4$ and $-2$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339524 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339524 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2d5a1f0b-7284-5bbc-b1e7-2ff8ad7d7d30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339629 #edb/ref 1080 "$-\\frac{13}{3}$ and $-\\frac{5}{3}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339629 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339629 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "37cbab4f-5a5d-53a0-989a-2bba919f1c6a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339731 #edb/ref 1080 "$-\\frac{7}{2}$ and $-\\frac{5}{2}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339731 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186339731 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "444fa7d9-40fd-53f5-9b43-5cab17eacd5b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340763 #edb/ref 1080 "$(0,\\sqrt{6})$ and $(0,-\\sqrt{6})$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340763 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186340763 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b3e77b72-b0aa-5aa2-80c3-74d69e6d1bde" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341189 #edb/ref 1080 "$(0,\\sqrt{6})$ and $(0,-2\\sqrt{3})$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341189 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341189 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e98d2c48-e98a-5bd8-bf7e-745db4c2794a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341246 #edb/ref 1080 "$-5$ and $-1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341246 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341246 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f0a5235b-49d2-541d-b7c7-7db7eaa4f152" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341250 #edb/ref 1080 "$(0,2\\sqrt{3})$ and $(0,-2\\sqrt{3})$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341250 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341250 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f0c3edd0-3761-5700-a2bb-55bbe3d60703" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341427 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339439 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341427 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341427 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339629 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341427 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341427 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186341246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341427 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341427 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341427 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186339524 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341427 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "1a6157a6-9ea9-521a-b21f-1bebe23c029e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341716 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339346 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341716 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186339410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341716 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186340763 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341716 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186341189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341716 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186341250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341716 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341716 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341716 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186339410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186341716 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c1b9401a-2720-53ab-b421-d5879f6deca9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342087 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341427 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342087 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73831" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342087 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342087 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/0a/0a9d728a5927f380bbc88445c6a409974d94050040f23000cce50f70de436917.png)\n\nWhat are the $x$-intercepts of the parabola shown above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342087 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9fb00539-5721-5d8a-80d7-0dcf285c8845" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342087 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-3,-1)$ and passes through the point $(-6,8).$\n\nThe general standard equation of an up- or down-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(x-h)^{2}=4p(y-k).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(-3,-1)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2} & =4p(y+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-6,8),$ we substitute $x=-6$ and $y=8$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-6+3)^{2} & =4p(8+1) \\\\ 9 & =4p(9) \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2} & =(y+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)^{2} & =(0+1) \\\\ x+3 & =\\pm 1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercepts are $-4$ and $-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342092 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341716 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342092 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73847" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342092 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342092 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the points of intersection of the parabola ${y}^{2}=3(x-2)$ with the $y$-axis." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342092 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "6253cbd5-f5b5-5898-ac4f-5142a7aaca73" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186342092 #edb/ref 1074 "When the parabola intersects the $y$-axis, we must have $x=0.$ So, we set $x=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =3(0-2) \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, as the equation ${y}^{2}=-6$ has no solutions, we conclude that there are no intersection points." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376983 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186376984 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376983 #edb/ref 1069 "q-251694" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376983 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376983 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/7e/7e3d4078888350baccee76e73ab9b4a80d2ec95359fbe965bef3dd6a07e5c3b5.png)\n\nThe value of the $x$-intercept of the parabola shown above is{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376983 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7ed7cc33-cf3b-5b34-a2ab-03c46db15415" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376983 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(-6,4)$ and passes through the point $(-4,8).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(-6,4)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n(y-4)^{2}=4p(x+6).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(-4,8),$ we substitute $x=-4$ and $y=8$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(8-4)^{2} & =4p(-4+6) \\\\ (4)^{2} & =4p\\cdot (2) \\\\ 16 & =8p \\\\ p & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =8(x+6).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-4)^{2} & =8(x+6) \\\\ 16 & =8(x+6) \\\\ 2 & =x+6 \\\\ x & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $-4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376984 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376984 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376984 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376984 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186376985 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376984 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "44eeaa7e-95d0-594d-b1b9-89222d742f44" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376985 #edb/ref 1080 "-4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376985 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376985 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b18a44d7-d4b0-55cb-86af-0e13704b8df9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376986 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186376987 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376986 #edb/ref 1069 "q-251697" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376986 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376986 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/fd/fd628bef568023d079cff41ed68efae949a0259822d79273671f633036e743ca.png)\n\nThe value of the $x$-intercept of the parabola shown above is{{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376986 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "05525262-11b5-5c22-9660-edbf983c26e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376986 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we need to find the equation of the parabola. From the diagram, we see that the parabola has a vertex at $(3,2)$ and passes through the point $(21,-4).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a left- or right-opening parabola with vertex $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(y-k)^{2}=4p(x-h).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $(h,k)=(3,2)$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n{(y-2)}^{2}=4p(x-3).\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find $p.$ Since the parabola passes through the point $(21,-4),$ we substitute $x=21$ and $y=-4$ into the equation and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(-4-2)}^{2} & =4p(21-3) \\\\ {(-6)}^{2} & =4p\\cdot (18) \\\\ 36 & =72p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =2(x-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhen the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the parabola and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(0-2)^{2} & =2(x-3) \\\\ 4 & =2(x-3) \\\\ 2 & =x-3 \\\\ x & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376987 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186376988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376987 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376987 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376987 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186376988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376987 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e3a3dacb-4323-51ba-b4c3-d89cd23af82b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376988 #edb/ref 1080 "5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376988 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186376988 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2b4f84fb-e01c-5de9-8a75-f717912ae5de" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
